  Inputs:
  - name: Hinpuwebcam
    style: Header
    label: Webcam
  - name: Inpuinputswebcamuse
    style: Menu
    label: Use
    default: 'off'
    menuNames:
    - 'off'
    - movement
    - body
    - test
    menuLabels:
    - 'Off'
    - Movement Only
    - Body Tracking
    - Test (No Webcam)
    help: 'What the webcam is for. Off: nothing opens it, camera and pose signals are 0. Movement Only: camera motion signals (light, no MediaPipe). Body Tracking: MediaPipe tracks the dancer (pose signals, body mask) and the camera motion signals work too. Test: a moving test pattern and a made-up dancer, no webcam needed. Read Status below to see if it works.'
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Webcamuse
  - name: Inpuinputscameradevice
    style: Menu
    label: Webcam
    default: V1|||\\?\usb#vid_30c9&pid_00ac&mi_00#6&198797cf&1&0000#{65e8773d-8f56-11d0-a3b9-00a0c9223196}\global|||0|||0|||Integrated Camera
    menuSource: me.parent().op('inputs').par.Cameradevice
    help: The one webcam the project uses, for camera motion, body tracking and the Camera instrument. Close other apps that use it.
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Cameradevice
  - name: Inpuinputswebcamstatus
    style: Str
    label: Status
    readOnly: true
    help: 'Read only: what the webcam is doing right now, and what to do if it is not working. The same line shows on pose_monitor.'
    value: 'Off: the webcam is not used.'
  - name: Inpuinputscamerasensitivity
    style: Float
    label: Sensitivity
    default: 10
    clampMin: true
    normMax: 50.0
    help: Multiplies the amount of movement seen. Raise it if camera_motion stays small; signals are clamped to 0-1 by the input assignment ranges.
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Camerasensitivity
  - name: Hinpuwearables
    style: Header
    label: Wearables
  - name: Inpuinputsserialenable
    style: Toggle
    label: Read Serial
    help: 'Read lines of text from a serial (USB) device such as the wireless receiver. Off when the project opens: turn it on once the receiver is plugged in and its Port is picked. Missing and Bluetooth ports are never opened (see Status).'
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Serialenable
  - name: Inpuinputsserialport
    style: StrMenu
    label: Port
    menuSource: me.parent().op('inputs').par.Serialport
    help: Serial port of the device (COM3 on Windows, /dev/cu.usbmodem... on macOS). The menu lists the ports TouchDesigner can see.
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Serialport
  - name: Inpuinputsserialstatus
    style: Str
    label: Status
    readOnly: true
    help: 'What Read Serial is doing now. A missing port or a Bluetooth port is never opened (either froze TouchDesigner), so a wrong Port is safe: pick the receiver and reading starts within a second.'
    value: 'Off'
  - name: Inpuinputswearable1
    style: Toggle
    label: Use Wearable 1
    default: true
    help: 'On: wearable 1''s signals (serial_w1_...) reach the mappings and wearable_monitor. Off: they are dropped, as if that wearable were switched off. Each group turns on only its own wearable.'
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Wearable1
  - name: Inpuinputswearable2
    style: Toggle
    label: Use Wearable 2
    default: true
    help: 'On: wearable 2''s signals (serial_w2_...) reach the mappings and wearable_monitor. Off: they are dropped, as if that wearable were switched off. Each group turns on only its own wearable.'
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Wearable2
  - name: Inpuinputswearable3
    style: Toggle
    label: Use Wearable 3
    default: true
    help: 'On: wearable 3''s signals (serial_w3_...) reach the mappings and wearable_monitor. Off: they are dropped, as if that wearable were switched off. Each group turns on only its own wearable.'
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Wearable3
  - name: Inpuinputsserialbaud
    style: Int
    label: Baud Rate
    default: 9600
    min: 300.0
    clampMin: true
    normMin: 9600.0
    normMax: 921600.0
    help: 'Must match the device: 921600 for the wireless receiver (NodeMCU), 115200 for a wearable plugged in by USB, or Serial.begin(...) in your own sketch.'
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Serialbaud
  - name: Inpuinputsserialnames
    style: Str
    label: Value Names
    help: 'Names for lines of plain numbers, in order, e.g. "accel, zone" turns "0.5,1" into serial_accel and serial_zone. Blank: serial_1, serial_2 ... Lines of name=value pairs name themselves.'
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Serialnames
  - name: Hinpubody
    style: Header
    label: Body Tracking
  - name: Inpuinputsposezones
    style: Int
    label: Stage Zones
    default: 3
    min: 1.0
    max: 5.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: 1.0
    normMax: 5.0
    help: How many equal zones pose_x is split into, left to right (1-5). pose_zone says which one the dancer is in (1 = left), and pose_zone1 ... pose_zone5 are 1 in that zone. Shown on pose_monitor.
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Posezones
  - name: Inpuinputsposeflipx
    style: Toggle
    label: Flip Left/Right
    help: 'Off: pose_x is 0 at the left of the MediaPipe picture, 1 at the right. On: reversed. Use it to match pose_x to the stage as the audience sees it.'
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Poseflipx
  - name: Inpuinputsposemask
    style: Toggle
    label: Body Mask
    help: 'Off (default): body tracking only, steadiest tracking. On: MediaPipe also finds the dancer''s outline (a body mask) for the Video Feedback instrument''s Echo: Dancer. It roughly halves how often MediaPipe updates the body (measured: 14 to 9 times a second, with gaps up to 2 s), so turn it on only when you use Echo: Dancer.'
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Posemask
  - name: Inpuinputsposesmooth
    style: Float
    label: Smoothing (s)
    default: 0.1
    clampMin: true
    help: 'Time in seconds that pose signals take to follow the dancer. Raise it if values jitter, lower it if they feel late. 0: no smoothing.'
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Posesmooth
  - name: Inpuinputsposesensitivity
    style: Float
    label: Energy Sensitivity
    default: 1
    clampMin: true
    normMax: 5.0
    help: Multiplies pose_energy. Raise it if pose_energy stays small during big movement.
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Posesensitivity
  - name: Inpuinputsposehold
    style: Float
    label: Hold When Lost (s)
    default: 0.5
    clampMin: true
    normMax: 2.0
    help: When MediaPipe loses the dancer for less than this many seconds, the pose signals keep their last values; after that they drop to 0.
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Posehold
  - name: Inpuinputsposezonemargin
    style: Float
    label: Zone Margin
    default: 0.05
    max: 0.2
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMax: 0.2
    help: 'How far past a zone border (fraction of the picture width) the dancer must go before the zone changes. Stops flicker when standing on a border. 0: change exactly at the border.'
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Posezonemargin
  - name: Hinputest
    style: Header
    label: Test Signals
  - name: Inpuinputssimlevel
    style: Float
    label: Level (sim_level)
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    help: 'Simulated continuous movement value 0-1, as a sensor would send. Signal name: sim_level.'
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Simlevel
  - name: Inpuinputssimtrigger
    style: Momentary
    label: Trigger (sim_trigger)
    help: 'Simulated momentary trigger: 1 while held, else 0. Signal name: sim_trigger.'
  - name: Inpuinputssimzone
    style: Toggle
    label: Zone (sim_zone)
    help: 'Simulated spatial zone: on = a dancer is in the zone. Signal name: sim_zone.'
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Simzone
  - name: Inpuinputssimanimate
    style: Toggle
    label: Animate Level
    help: Move sim_level up and down automatically (slow sine wave), to test mappings without touching the slider.
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Simanimate
  - name: Hinpuosc
    style: Header
    label: OSC
  - name: Inpuinputsoscenable
    style: Toggle
    label: Receive OSC
    help: Listen for OSC messages (UDP) on the port below. Each OSC address becomes a signal, e.g. /dancer/level -> dancer/level. Off by default.
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Oscenable
  - name: Inpuinputsoscport
    style: Int
    label: OSC Port
    default: 7000
    min: 1.0
    max: 65535.0
    clampMin: true
    clampMax: true
    normMin: 1000.0
    normMax: 12000.0
    help: UDP port to listen on. The sending app or device must send to this computer on this port.
    value: ~me.parent().op('inputs').par.Oscport
parameters:
  parentshortcut: Control
  opshortcut: Control
sequences:
  ext:
  - object: op('./ControlExt').module.ControlExt(me)
    name: Control
    promote: true
color: [0.3, 0.5, 0.9]
tags:
- tdxn
storage:
  _pageNames:
    show: Show
    phases: Phases
    instruments: Instruments
    composition: Composition
    movement: Movement
    inputs: Inputs
operators:
- name: layout
  type: tableDAT
  parameters:
    file: project1/control/layout.tsv
    syncfile: true
    rows: 176
    cols: 5
  position: [0, -200]
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.9, 0.3, 0.4]
  tags:
  - tsv
- name: ControlExt
  type: textDAT
  parameters:
    file: project1/control/ControlExt.py
    syncfile: true
    language: python
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.9, 0.3, 0.4]
  tags:
  - py
- name: control_pulses
  type: parameterexecuteDAT
  parameters:
    fromop: =parent()
    op: ..
    pars: Mode Showtransportreset Showtransportseek Showvisualsopenwindow Showvisualsclosewindow Phasphasessaveshow Phasphasesloadshow Instparticlesreset Instvideoreset Instnoisereset Insttilesrefresh Instmediarefresh Compmediachoosefolder
    builtin: false
    file: project1/control/control_pulses.py
    syncfile: true
  position: [0, -400]
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.9, 0.3, 0.4]
  tags:
  - py
- name: status_refresh
  type: executeDAT
  parameters:
    fromop: =parent()
    framestart: true
  position: [0, -600]
  size: [130, 90]
  color: [0.67, 0.67, 0.67]
  dat_content: "\"\"\"status_refresh: copies the panel's status lines and playback position a few times a second (ControlExt.refreshStatus).\"\"\"\n\n\ndef onFrameStart(frame):\n\tif frame % 15 == 0:\n\t\top.Control.ext.Control.refreshStatus()\n"
  dat_content_format: text
annotations:
- name: annotate1
  mode: annotate
  title: Control panel
  text: layout lists every control (tab, section, component, parameter, Basic, instrument). Edit it, then op.Control.Rebuild(). ControlExt binds each control to its parameter; control_pulses rebuilds on Mode / Instrument and forwards pulses.
  position: [-70, -470]
  size: [270, 730]
  color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
